add('The [UR5e datasheet](https://www.universal-robots.com/media/1807465/ur5e_e-series_datasheets_web.pdf) provides the5 kg payload curve through approximately350 mm CoG offset and permits any mounting orientation. The current [SW5.23 specification](https://www.universal-robots.com/manuals/EN/HTML/SW5_23/Content/prod-usr-man/complianceUR5e/H_g5_sections/appendix_g5/tech_spec_sheet.htm) is conservatively covered by a151 mm base reservation and ±160° elbow limit in these new searches. Archived solids/inertias are retained, rather than claiming a perfect current-revision CAD match. [xArm manual](https://www.ufactory.cc/wp-content/uploads/2023/05/xArm-User-Manual-V2.0.0.pdf), [UR3e](https://www.universal-robots.com/products/ur3e/). Home-tier arm power-loss holding evidence and de-energize-to-apply rail braking remain the design basis.')
add('**Rotato is rejected**, because its manual forbids programmable-device operation. The replacement is a **custom guarded linear peeling station**, not a claimed turnkey commodity peeler: the existing full peeling tool and unchanged63 N tangential/7.5 N normal process forces are retained. A buyable **Actuonix P16-200-256-12-P** drives a guided stroke. Its200 mm travel and247 mm closed hole spacing fit a full480 ×50 ×50 mm drive/guide cover. Separate guide bearings take the radial load, since the actuator200 mm variant allows only4 N side load. Full guards, a360 ×200 ×6 mm lid, handle, hinge and scrap floor remain modeled. The recipe and food-quality assumption do not certify the custom holder, guard sweep or mechanism.')
add('The [P16 product](https://www.actuonix.com/p16-200-256-12-p) and [OEM datasheet](https://www.actuonix.com/assets/images/datasheets/ActuonixP16Datasheet.pdf) specify12 V,300 N maximum force,500 N static/backdrive holding, and150 N at3.4 mm/s. The datasheet expressly allows automatic position control with DPDT relay/H-bridge or LAC control. This addresses the Rotato programming prohibition. Six160 mm out-and-return passes at3.4 mm/s, respecting the20% duty limit, give a **2,823.53 s design allowance per root** including cooling. This is derived from actuator data, not a measured peeling cycle; blade indexing and quality remain declared design assumptions. The inherited force evidence is retained, including the [robotic peeling research](https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.06570).')
